WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.805
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:15.147
Unit seven: Staying Safe Online. In this unit, you will give advice about online safety.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.116
Online.

5
00:00:17.816 --> 00:00:19.920
Online means connected to the internet.

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.557
I play games online with my cousin.

7
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:26.153
Your turn. Say: Online.

8
00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:29.714
Online.

9
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:31.555
Password.

10
00:00:32.255 --> 00:00:34.789
Password means a secret word for your account.

11
00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:36.787
Use a strong password.

12
00:00:37.487 --> 00:00:40.232
Your turn. Say: Password.

13
00:00:42.932 --> 00:00:43.863
Password.

14
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:45.677
Private.

15
00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:49.108
Private means only for you, not for everyone.

16
00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:50.792
Keep your address private.

17
00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:54.249
Your turn. Say: Private.

18
00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:57.799
Private.

19
00:00:58.783 --> 00:00:59.750
Stranger.

20
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.414
Stranger means a person you don't know.

21
00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:04.516
Don't chat with strangers online.

22
00:01:05.216 --> 00:01:08.206
Your turn. Say: Stranger.

23
00:01:10.906 --> 00:01:11.883
Stranger.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:13.733
Share.

25
00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:17.582
Share means to let other people see or use something.

26
00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:19.580
Think before you share a photo.

27
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.607
Your turn. Say: Share.

28
00:01:25.307 --> 00:01:26.123
Share.

29
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.036
Report.

30
00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:31.479
Report means to tell someone in charge about a problem.

31
00:01:31.779 --> 00:01:33.512
Report unkind messages.

32
00:01:34.212 --> 00:01:37.363
Your turn. Say: Report.

33
00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:40.960
Report.

34
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.707
Block.

35
00:01:43.407 --> 00:01:46.231
Block means to stop someone from contacting you.

36
00:01:46.531 --> 00:01:48.078
You can block that account.

37
00:01:48.778 --> 00:01:51.198
Your turn. Say: Block.

38
00:01:53.898 --> 00:01:54.679
Block.

39
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:56.464
Safe.

40
00:01:57.164 --> 00:01:58.896
Safe means not in danger.

41
00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:00.662
Stay safe online.

42
00:02:01.362 --> 00:02:03.480
Your turn. Say: Safe.

43
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:06.914
Safe.

44
00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:09.905
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:10.205 --> 00:02:13.284
Sreypich, what should you do if a stranger messages you?

46
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:17.108
I shouldn't answer. I should tell an adult.

47
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:19.987
And if someone is unkind?

48
00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:23.155
I should block and report them.

49
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.950
What should you keep private?

50
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.863
My password, my address and my school's name.

51
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.440
Grammar focus: Should and shouldn't.

52
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.391
You should keep your password private. You shouldn't share your address.

53
00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:43.720
Good online advice is short and clear: should for safe actions, shouldn't for risky ones.

54
00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:48.379
Now read and listen. Safe Online, Happy Online.

55
00:02:48.679 --> 00:02:51.770
The internet is useful and fun, but we must be careful.

56
00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:55.988
When I'm online, I keep my password private.

57
00:02:57.283 --> 00:03:00.096
I never share personal information with a stranger.

58
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:04.823
If someone is unkind, I block and report them and tell an adult.

59
00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:09.091
Being safe online helps everyone enjoy the internet.

60
00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:12.931
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.231 --> 00:03:15.277
You blank share your address online.

62
00:03:15.577 --> 00:03:19.300
A, shouldn't. B, should. C, must.

63
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:25.351
The answer is A: shouldn't.

64
00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.699
A person you don't know is a blank.

65
00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:32.222
A, stranger. B, friend. C, teacher.

66
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:37.891
The answer is A: stranger.

67
00:03:39.383 --> 00:03:42.079
To stop someone from contacting you is to blank.

68
00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:45.592
A, block. B, share. C, post.

69
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:51.351
The answer is A: block.

70
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:57.267
Now it's your turn to speak. What should you do if a stranger messages you online?

71
00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:07.251
I shouldn't reply. I should block the stranger and tell my parents or my teacher.

72
00:04:07.551 --> 00:04:09.353
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:14.117
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should and shouldn't.

74
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:19.101
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

75
00:04:19.401 --> 00:04:21.670
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

76
00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.890
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

